[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"395","stub":{"id":"395","section":"01. Tabernash to Granby","altname":"","river":"Fraser","difficulty":"IIItoIV","states":["USA-COL"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":{"status":"below-recommended","latestReading":{"value":"29","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:15:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null},"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":"There are now two put-ins to access the Fraser on Ranch Creek. Both are on private property - being respectful is paramount to maintaining access to this valuable local resource. First access is from the bridge. Parking is limited and beaver dams can pose a hazard. Second access is from the Phases parking lot and bypasses the first few dams.","id":"109640","location":{"latitude":"39.9987","longitude":"-105.843"},"name":"Put In","distance":"0","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"takeout","description":"Park at the Granby fire station. Small access points on either side of the diversion riffle (runnable). During peak season, quickly make way for others to land.","id":"114890","location":{"latitude":"40.0815","longitude":"-105.929"},"name":"Take Out","distance":"9.4","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false}],"alerts":[],"photos":[{"id":"CBdp1BjCVTdL4oZ64xzfI","ext":"jpg","post_id":"m1j0A1Da1RByOLEmSIxVP","description":"","caption":"Thumper ","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Keegan Lape","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2023-06-23T08:07:27.000Z","updated_at":"2023-06-27T08:07:27.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/CBdp1BjCVTdL4oZ64xzfI","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/CBdp1BjCVTdL4oZ64xzfI"}}],"detail":{"id":"395","permitUrl":null,"permitInfo":null,"description":"The Fraser is an exciting and dynamic canyon which laregly feels like creek boating. The only public land is from the confluence of Ranch Creek and the Fraser to the tunnel. The next public land is at the takeout. Do not stop on private land.\n\nRead and run  until Thumper (III-IV) ~ 1.5 miles past the tunnel bridge which marks the end of public land. Scout river left - fast landing at a tree-less scramble to the tracks - or read and run. Higher flows can be more foregiving. The preferred run is right with a pull off Thumper rock. Read and run rapids (I-II+) follow intermittently for the next ~2 - 2.5 miles. The runout behind Granby Ranch is calm and winding. Where braided, avoid the left no-go channel. Be prepared to encounter deadfall across parts or all of the river at any time.\n\nRecommend using this guage to assess flow in the canyon: [https://dwr.state.co.us/Tools/Stations/FRAGRACO?params=DISCHRG](https://dwr.state.co.us/Tools/Stations/FRAGRACO?params=DISCHRG)   (or combine Fraser @ Tabernash with Ranch Creek on USGS). Small boats can run this stretch at significantly lower flows.","averageGradient":"34","maxGradient":null,"length":"9.9","correlations":[{"reachID":"395","isPrimary":false,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"cfs","belowRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableRangeComment":null,"mediumRunnableRangeComment":null,"highRunnableRangeComment":null,"aboveRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"highRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"beginLowRunnable":"300","beginMediumRunnable":null,"beginHighRunnable":null,"endHighRunnable":"2000"},"gaugeInfo":{"name":"FRASER RIVER AT TABERNASH, CO","gaugeSource":"USGS","gaugeSourceIdentifier":"09027100","gaugeFetchStatus":"ACTIVE","latestFlowReading":{"value":"13","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:15:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"latestStageReading":{"value":"3.32","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:15:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"location":{"latitude":"39.990333","longitude":"-105.829778"},"externalSourceLinks":{"sourceLink":{"url":"https://water.noaa.gov/gauges/09027100","text":"NOAA"},"secondaryLink":{"url":"https://waterdata.usgs.gov/monitoring-location/09027100/#parameterCode=00060&period=P7D","te